    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\n3-Bedroom Terraced Home conveniently located between Camp and Castlegregory.\n\nThis well presented terraced property offers contemporary living in a well-maintained development with excellent curb appeal. Finished to a high standard, the property creates a warm and inviting atmosphere.\n\nThe stunning views of Tralee Bay are magnificient and will impress all discerning purchasers.\n\nThe property boasts a total floor area of 1550sq/ft. The ground floor features a living room, a fully fitted kitchen with dining area and utility along with a downstairs W.C and there is access to a small private back patio area. \n\nUpstairs, there are three very spacious bedrooms one of which is En-suite along with a family bathroom and hot press.\n\nThe bedroom space will easily accommodate eight people which is ideal for a larger family unit seeking an idyllic holiday home.\n\nLarge double-glazed windows throughout ensure plenty of natural light, while the exterior features attractive stone detailing, a slate roof, and a neatly paved forecourt with communal parking to the front. The property benefits from oil-fired central heating, a stove in the living area, and boasts an excellent B2 energy rating.\n\nSituated close to a range of local amenities, schools, and transport links, this property presents an excellent opportunity for first-time buyers, investors, or anyone seeking a stylish, low-maintenance home in a highly desirable location.\n\nEnjoy the convenience of being just a 5-minute drive from the village of Castlegregory, 26 minutes from the town of Tralee, and 34 minutes from the coast of Dingle, offering the perfect blend of tranquility and accessibility to some of Kerry's most scenic destinations.\n\nThe property forms part of a managed development, with an annual management fee of approximately 1,000 contributing to the upkeep of communal areas and shared facilities, ensuring the surroundings remain beautifully maintained year-round."
      },
